WEBVTT

00:01.690 --> 00:04.890
It's July, and our term finals
are in the rear view.

00:04.890 --> 00:07.730
I hope you're all doing well
back in Ikajima.

00:07.730 --> 00:09.670
Finally done!

00:10.470 --> 00:14.860
Just for today, I'll stop
worrying about my grades

00:14.860 --> 00:16.870
A movie means we could all go.

00:15.200 --> 00:18.210
and the other stuff bothering me...

00:16.870 --> 00:19.350
What? Karaoke sounds like a better idea.

00:22.550 --> 00:27.290
I think this is the first time
I've ever been real friends with a girl.

00:28.380 --> 00:31.740
I'm feeling like forgetting all about them!

00:33.060 --> 00:33.800
See you.

00:33.060 --> 00:36.010
But it's not all fun and games.

00:33.800 --> 00:36.010
Yeah, bye-bye!

00:36.420 --> 00:40.010
There's a student council
roundtable after school today.

00:40.610 --> 00:45.390
I apologize for not letting you know
sooner, but I, Iwakura Mitsumi,

00:45.390 --> 00:49.570
have officially been appointed student
council secretary for the first term!

00:51.350 --> 00:54.730
So dazzling

00:54.730 --> 00:58.170
I find myself looking away

00:58.890 --> 01:01.790
Unable to find the right words

01:01.790 --> 01:04.580
Even a single word to say

01:18.920 --> 01:21.650
In such a narrow world

01:21.650 --> 01:25.430
Your vibrant laughter

01:25.430 --> 01:28.400
Resonates so beautifully

01:28.400 --> 01:31.210
And that's what saved me

01:31.650 --> 01:35.310
If we relive this moment

01:35.310 --> 01:38.530
In an unimaginable future

01:38.530 --> 01:41.500
Even if we're lost, it's okay

01:41.500 --> 01:45.340
We will be in it together

01:46.030 --> 01:49.330
So dazzling

01:49.330 --> 01:53.130
I find myself looking away

01:53.500 --> 01:56.420
Unable to find the right words

01:56.420 --> 01:59.250
Even a single word to say

01:59.250 --> 02:02.580
I was entranced

02:02.580 --> 02:06.690
By your lively figure

02:06.690 --> 02:09.840
If the true nature of this blue warmth

02:09.840 --> 02:12.620
Is love, then…

02:13.350 --> 02:16.480
If the true nature of this blue warmth

02:16.480 --> 02:19.260
Is love, then...

02:20.990 --> 02:23.990
Student Council
Roundtable Discussion
Agenda
Things about Tsubame West
that are fine as they are
and those that need an update.
All students across all years are free to join.
Hope to see you there!

02:20.990 --> 02:23.990
Starts 15:10, 7/11,
2F Meeting Room B

02:35.020 --> 02:38.010
I'd like to end the roundtable on that note.

02:38.010 --> 02:40.780
As for the new student
council president, naturally,

02:40.760 --> 02:47.220
Second-Year
Takamine Tokiko

02:41.260 --> 02:43.160
Takamine-senpai...

02:43.160 --> 02:47.220
Thanks to you all, we've had
another productive discussion.

02:47.730 --> 02:52.020
Now, the closing address
if you would, please, President.

02:52.330 --> 02:54.600
...was the clear favorite in my mind.

02:55.770 --> 03:00.280
New Student Council President
Second-Year
Kazakami Hiroto

02:55.770 --> 03:00.280
Vice President

02:55.770 --> 03:00.280
Thank you all for joining us today.

03:00.730 --> 03:05.140
The all-new student council
is raring to get to work.

03:05.140 --> 03:10.450
And we'd like to take your ideas into
account and make our school even better.

03:12.390 --> 03:16.620
I'm sure you're all worn out from the exams,
so I think I'll cut my speech short there!

03:17.580 --> 03:19.160
Great work today.

03:19.160 --> 03:21.010
Go home and get some rest.

03:25.030 --> 03:26.520
Mitsumi-kun.

03:27.220 --> 03:31.230
Drama Club Incoming President
Second-Year
Kanechika Narumi

03:27.740 --> 03:31.230
Congrats on officially
joining the student council!

03:31.230 --> 03:34.360
Kanechika-senpai! Thank you very much.

03:34.360 --> 03:35.610
I'll grab this end.

03:36.320 --> 03:39.600
I didn't know you took part in roundtables.

03:39.600 --> 03:43.610
Believe it or not, I've never missed
one that didn't overlap with club.

03:43.610 --> 03:47.160
After all, great ideas are born
from such communication.

03:48.200 --> 03:50.410
Oh, Takamine-kun!

03:50.900 --> 03:53.510
It's a shame how the presidential
election turned out.

03:53.510 --> 03:56.160
But being vice president
is nothing to sneeze at.

03:56.160 --> 03:57.040
Thank you.

03:57.040 --> 04:02.420
If anything, the vice president
may shoulder more responsibilities.

04:02.910 --> 04:06.680
In any field, the right-hand man
is a crucial position.

04:06.680 --> 04:08.850
Anyway, I'm rooting for you,

04:08.850 --> 04:10.480
Vice President!

04:14.310 --> 04:15.770
Mi... Mitsumi-san.

04:16.240 --> 04:17.510
I leave the rest to you!

04:19.480 --> 04:23.800
Mitsumi-kun... Was I perhaps
being really insensitive just now?

04:26.490 --> 04:32.460
Kanechika-senpai, Takamine-senpai's
wounds are still very fresh.

04:33.960 --> 04:38.670
Student Council Office

04:35.920 --> 04:38.670
A Day in June

04:37.810 --> 04:40.970
Thank you, Tsubame Society.

04:38.670 --> 04:41.420
Student General Assembly

04:41.420 --> 04:44.580
The upcoming general assembly will mark
the end of us third-years' term in office.

04:44.580 --> 04:46.580
We'll do our best with this material.

04:46.580 --> 04:47.930
Thank you so much, really.

04:48.330 --> 04:49.380
Thank you!

04:49.380 --> 04:50.560
A job well done!

04:50.560 --> 04:51.930
Thank you for your service.

04:54.440 --> 04:56.820
We'll miss you.

04:56.820 --> 04:59.520
I can rest easy knowing my
successor will do a good job.

04:59.520 --> 05:01.340
Counting on you, Takamine.

05:01.340 --> 05:02.820
Of course!

05:02.820 --> 05:06.640
Yesterday was the deadline for
the presidential candidacies, right?

05:07.280 --> 05:10.560
It sounds like I was the only one,
so it'll go to a vote of confidence.

05:10.560 --> 05:12.330
It's too bad. I was hoping to compete.

05:12.330 --> 05:15.860
Oh, someone else entered
just before the deadline.

05:15.860 --> 05:16.540
Huh?

05:17.070 --> 05:20.960
Oh, really? But given my track
record, I should be able to...

05:20.960 --> 05:22.300
It's Kazakami-kun, the second-year.

05:22.660 --> 05:25.310
Huh... I wonder what he's like...

05:27.630 --> 05:30.050
Kazakami-senpai from second-year, huh?

05:30.050 --> 05:31.930
A formidable foe appears.

05:31.930 --> 05:34.910
Damn, Mika-chan, you know everything.

05:34.910 --> 05:36.710
Well, duh, he's famous.

05:36.710 --> 05:39.020
Like, Shima-kun famous.

05:39.020 --> 05:40.190
Oh.

05:40.190 --> 05:43.140
He was in line to be
the soccer team's captain,

05:43.140 --> 05:45.230
but he quit after an injury this spring.

05:45.230 --> 05:47.650
Maybe he wanted to try something new?

05:47.650 --> 05:49.070
Oh, I see.

05:49.070 --> 05:52.100
He must be a good leader
if he was in line to be captain,

05:52.100 --> 05:54.740
which means the guys will vote for him.

05:54.740 --> 05:56.590
So will the girls. In droves!

05:56.590 --> 06:00.580
But Takamine-senpai has been
on the council since her first year!

06:00.580 --> 06:04.970
I mean, we know she's dedicated
because you've told us,

06:04.970 --> 06:07.880
but it can be hard to tell from the outside.

06:07.880 --> 06:12.260
Honestly, Takamine-senpai seems
too serious and kinda scary.

06:12.260 --> 06:15.580
She'll have a tough time
against one of the populars.

06:16.640 --> 06:20.770
No! No one is more invested
in the school's affairs than she is!

06:20.770 --> 06:23.880
And a leader has to be tough at times!

06:23.880 --> 06:26.750
I'm sure a lot of people get that!

06:26.400 --> 06:27.900
Translation: Right?!

06:26.750 --> 06:27.900
Don'cha reckon?!

06:29.070 --> 06:30.200
Reckon?

06:32.700 --> 06:36.040
You are hereby elected
the new student council president.

06:41.870 --> 06:43.250
Senpai...

06:46.260 --> 06:48.420
Well, what's done is done.

06:48.850 --> 06:52.510
Kazakami-san was forced to give up soccer,
something he'd devoted himself to.

06:53.110 --> 06:56.620
I'm sure he'll direct his energies
to his presidential duties.

06:57.750 --> 06:58.930
That's why...

06:58.930 --> 07:03.680
I'm thinking of giving him this
"things to do as president" notebook!

06:58.980 --> 06:59.020
When I Become President
Takamine Tokiko

07:03.680 --> 07:07.980
I've been keeping notes in it
since I was a first-year.

07:07.980 --> 07:09.700
That's amazing, Senpai!

07:10.760 --> 07:13.000
My brother had the same injury.

07:13.000 --> 07:15.870
If you've recovered that much,
you could've made it back by next year.

07:16.240 --> 07:17.950
Honestly, yeah.

07:17.950 --> 07:21.500
But I never intended to be
in a club as a third-year anyway.

07:21.500 --> 07:23.240
What? Really?!

07:23.240 --> 07:26.780
Student council terms are up
within the year, which is perfect.

07:26.780 --> 07:29.540
And it puts me on the teachers'
radar in a good way.

07:29.540 --> 07:31.630
You sure do love to stand out.

07:33.100 --> 07:35.890
Hey, I was born to lead, after all!

07:36.890 --> 07:39.630
You suck ass! Begone, himbo!

07:39.630 --> 07:40.690
He nailed it!

07:40.690 --> 07:43.270
He nailed the joke
I failed spectacularly with!

07:45.530 --> 07:46.690
Senpai?

07:46.690 --> 07:48.340
I'm a fool, aren't I?

07:48.340 --> 07:49.320
You're not!

07:51.320 --> 07:54.570
When I Become President
Takamine Tokiko

07:53.260 --> 07:54.570
But this...

07:56.170 --> 07:58.300
is all I can do...

08:00.330 --> 08:02.210
When I Become President
Takamine Tokiko

08:04.960 --> 08:09.710
I wanted to cheer her up, but I couldn't.

08:10.130 --> 08:13.520
But I've begun to realize
the same thing she has.

08:15.230 --> 08:19.220
Hard work builds confidence, but...

08:19.820 --> 08:25.960
It's scary that all we can do
is hope that it'll pay off someday.

08:32.440 --> 08:33.380
Later!

08:33.380 --> 08:34.610
Bye!

08:34.610 --> 08:36.470
You guys have day duties?

08:36.470 --> 08:40.870
Yeah. It's Takamine-senpai
and me on Tuesdays.

08:40.870 --> 08:42.930
Wow. Must be rough.

08:42.930 --> 08:44.170
Not at all.

08:44.170 --> 08:47.740
There's never much to do,
so I use the time to study.

08:47.740 --> 08:49.980
Oh, mind if I come?

08:49.980 --> 08:50.590
Huh?

08:50.590 --> 08:52.220
You study, right?

08:52.220 --> 08:54.550
I've got time to kill today, so is it okay?

08:54.960 --> 08:56.860
It's... probably fine.

08:56.860 --> 08:58.220
Yay!

08:58.770 --> 09:00.030
It's gone up.

09:00.030 --> 09:04.740
I think my friendship level's
gone up in his mind!

09:04.730 --> 09:07.480
Student Council Office

09:10.480 --> 09:12.950
Hello!

09:12.950 --> 09:14.860
Huh? Shima-kun?

09:16.170 --> 09:18.710
Excellent. I wanted you to see this too.

09:18.710 --> 09:19.370
See what?

09:28.600 --> 09:33.350
Dun... dun... duuun....

09:33.710 --> 09:38.430
Charley  Horse

09:35.180 --> 09:36.240
Charley?

09:36.240 --> 09:38.450
Charley horse? As in a leg cramp?

09:38.450 --> 09:41.830
I thought it was a clever name at the time.

09:41.830 --> 09:42.430
Hm?

09:42.430 --> 09:43.430
Producer: Kanechika Narumi
Concept: Kanechika Narumi

09:43.680 --> 09:45.180
Script: Kanechika Narumi
Filming: Kanechika Narumi

09:44.410 --> 09:46.060
Wait...

09:45.430 --> 09:46.060
Director: Kanechika Narumi

09:46.800 --> 09:48.200
Is this...

09:48.810 --> 09:50.780
Yes, I see it.

09:50.780 --> 09:53.080
Based on the elevation
of the mountain behind it,

09:53.080 --> 09:55.550
I estimate its head to be...

09:55.550 --> 09:59.390
It's my debut film from when
I wanted to be a movie director!

10:00.440 --> 10:02.060
I was in fifth grade.

10:02.060 --> 10:05.330
And because I had no friends,
I was a one-man cast and crew!

10:05.970 --> 10:10.760
This is the second time you've
asked me to watch something...

10:09.710 --> 10:11.590
This is extremely bad!

10:12.330 --> 10:15.240
I appreciate actual child actors more now.

10:15.240 --> 10:18.090
I think I know what you're trying to say.

10:18.620 --> 10:22.350
I was super into tokusatsu at the time,
so I ripped off the setting.

10:22.350 --> 10:26.350
The story's about a child prodigy, me,
contacting a famous paleontologist

10:26.350 --> 10:29.520
when he sees the kaiju Charley Horse.

10:29.520 --> 10:32.340
Doesn't saying it out loud embarrass him?

10:36.050 --> 10:38.280
Wait, are you actually really embarrassed?

10:38.280 --> 10:41.990
Of course I am! I'm sweating buckets here!

10:41.990 --> 10:44.080
Then why show it to us?

10:44.080 --> 10:46.120
Because, well...

10:46.490 --> 10:48.510
Isn't this hilarious?

10:48.510 --> 10:52.670
I know you guys are trying to be polite,
but it's okay to laugh!

10:52.670 --> 10:58.280
Of course, I want to create something
amazing someday and gain widespread acclaim.

10:58.280 --> 11:02.600
But between never showing this awful thing
to anyone and making you three laugh,

11:02.600 --> 11:04.300
I chose the latter.

11:09.370 --> 11:10.960
But it's okay!

11:10.960 --> 11:12.390
With Hyper Charley...

11:12.390 --> 11:17.450
With the super missile I developed
overnight, Hyper Charley EX,

11:17.450 --> 11:19.490
Charley Horse will be reduced to...

11:19.490 --> 11:21.700
Naru-kun! Naru-kun!

11:22.210 --> 11:24.750
Want some watermelon? Naru-kun!

11:24.750 --> 11:25.700
Shh! Shhh!

11:26.210 --> 11:27.250
Grandma brought... What?

11:27.250 --> 11:29.200
Dad, I'm filming right now!

11:29.450 --> 11:31.110
Oh, am I on camera?

11:31.570 --> 11:32.800
Yay! Peace, peace!

11:32.800 --> 11:34.200
Jeez!

11:34.840 --> 11:40.920
Student Council Office

11:35.460 --> 11:38.430
Okay, show's over! Everyone go home!

11:42.630 --> 11:44.090
Mitsumi-san!

11:44.730 --> 11:46.600
Takamine-senpai.

11:46.910 --> 11:49.380
The other day was fun, huh?

11:49.380 --> 11:50.750
Wasn't it?

11:51.590 --> 11:53.600
I laugh every time I think about it.

11:55.190 --> 11:59.860
You see, it helped me finally
come to terms with everything.

12:00.180 --> 12:01.410
That's great.

12:01.410 --> 12:05.030
What I'm lacking right now is
magnanimity and playfulness.

12:06.280 --> 12:07.490
Crammed

12:06.630 --> 12:10.920
So I tried making a list of everything from
daily relaxations to monthly indulgences.

12:07.490 --> 12:13.750
Crammed

12:10.920 --> 12:13.750
Whoa! I-I see...

12:15.250 --> 12:19.760
Be More Approachable
Wear bright colors and accessories.
Have a smile on my face normally.
When someone calls out to me,
stop whatever I'm doing
and talk to them.

12:19.760 --> 12:24.260
Goals for Summer Break
Invite Yamamori-san and
Tsukada-san to the festival.
Pick out three trendy places
I want to try going to.
Eggs Singer pancakes.
Might have to line up,
even on a weekday...
This may be an easy place
to start.

12:27.310 --> 12:29.510
That's wonderful! It's very you, Senpai!

12:30.790 --> 12:32.020
Thank you.

12:33.700 --> 12:34.770
Kazakami-san!

12:35.180 --> 12:36.300
Just who I wanted to see.

12:36.300 --> 12:37.200
Huh?

12:37.770 --> 12:41.030
I should have said this sooner.
I look forward to working with you.

12:42.580 --> 12:44.780
Oh, likewise.

12:45.250 --> 12:48.340
I hope to learn a lot from you, too.

12:48.780 --> 12:52.060
Do you want to go eat something
sweet sometime this week?

12:52.060 --> 12:55.410
Oh, my schedule's packed for this month.

12:55.410 --> 12:56.660
What was that all about?

12:57.540 --> 13:01.130
It couldn't hurt to
slack off once in a while.

13:01.130 --> 13:02.030
Slack off?!

13:02.920 --> 13:04.620
Maybe you're right.

13:04.620 --> 13:08.210
If my exam grades are good
enough, I'll consider it.

13:08.210 --> 13:09.250
Urk!

13:09.250 --> 13:10.850
I forgot all about those!

13:11.970 --> 13:15.980
Scene 07: Hectic and Hot Stuff

13:17.680 --> 13:19.990
Summer break's almost here, isn't it?

13:19.990 --> 13:20.990
Yeah.

13:20.990 --> 13:23.290
I can't wait to go home.

13:23.290 --> 13:26.120
Yeah, you didn't go back over Golden Week.

13:26.500 --> 13:29.460
I'll go to the beach every day!

13:29.460 --> 13:32.700
Stuff myself with tomatoes and watermelons!

13:33.080 --> 13:36.500
And maybe get my folks to
buy me a huge fireworks set!

13:36.500 --> 13:39.250
Sounds like a kid's schedule...

13:39.250 --> 13:42.390
I hope I can bring my school
friends to visit someday.

13:42.390 --> 13:44.130
Shima-kun says he likes the beach.

13:44.860 --> 13:47.630
Mitsu...? Uh...

13:47.630 --> 13:51.570
You talk about this Shima-kun an awful lot.

13:51.570 --> 13:55.390
D-Do I? He's a friend named
Shima Sousuke-kun.

13:55.910 --> 13:57.560
See you, Nao-chan.

13:57.560 --> 13:59.420
Take care!

14:00.900 --> 14:03.220
Shima... Sousuke.

14:03.220 --> 14:05.340
Just what kind of character is this guy?

14:05.650 --> 14:08.150
Shimasuke!

14:08.150 --> 14:10.160
Miyamaeyama

14:12.380 --> 14:14.660
Oh, it's Shima-kun.

14:21.530 --> 14:22.280
Oh.

14:23.990 --> 14:25.820
Morning, Mitsumi-chan.

14:25.820 --> 14:26.990
Good morning.

14:26.990 --> 14:28.800
Were you apologizing for something?

14:28.800 --> 14:31.540
Oh, she asked for my contact details.

14:32.300 --> 14:34.680
And, well... You know.

14:34.680 --> 14:36.440
So you said no.

14:36.440 --> 14:38.440
I've been trying to recently.

14:38.730 --> 14:42.740
I don't think she was asking
because she wanted to be friends...

14:42.740 --> 14:44.440
so I couldn't half-ass it.

14:44.790 --> 14:47.860
Oh, the regality of a popular person!

14:49.010 --> 14:51.700
Mitsumi-chan, are you gonna
go home over summer break?

14:51.700 --> 14:54.200
Yeah. I gotta bring gifts
for everyone back home.

14:54.520 --> 14:56.330
Like Fumi-chan, who gave you
the panda hairpins?

14:56.330 --> 14:58.710
Yeah! Good memory!

14:58.710 --> 15:01.850
I told her I'd go see Liang Liang and all.

15:01.850 --> 15:03.480
So I gotta go to the zoo

15:03.480 --> 15:08.360
and pick up a coin pouch, a handkerchief,
or other panda merch to pay her back.

15:08.360 --> 15:10.090
Oh, sounds good.

15:10.090 --> 15:13.990
Huh? But I think the zoo's gonna be
super crowded over summer break.

15:15.130 --> 15:17.970
I hadn't looked into that!

15:18.420 --> 15:20.160
Morning, Shima-kun.

15:20.610 --> 15:21.480
Morning.

15:21.480 --> 15:23.010
He's so cute.

15:23.010 --> 15:24.000
Friends?

15:24.000 --> 15:25.480
Nope. No idea who they are.

15:33.290 --> 15:35.170
Boys, it is <i>so</i> happening right now.

15:35.170 --> 15:37.930
The pre-summer-break popularity rush is here!

15:38.620 --> 15:41.040
That's Yagi-senpai, the Madonna
of the second-years.

15:41.620 --> 15:44.130
How I want to be you, Shima!

15:44.130 --> 15:45.420
Excuse me, Sensei.

15:45.420 --> 15:47.450
What do you mean by rush?

15:48.380 --> 15:52.110
It's elementary. Once summer break starts,
you won't see your crush for a while.

15:52.110 --> 15:57.390
So a lot of people start asking for
contact info or straight up ask them out!

15:57.940 --> 16:03.260
Why, I couldn't muster up the courage
to ask Kaori-chan, my middle school love.

16:03.260 --> 16:07.510
And then I found out she'd gotten
a boyfriend over summer break.

16:07.510 --> 16:09.030
S-Sensei!

16:09.030 --> 16:12.180
Even Shima couldn't say no
to a girl like that.

16:12.180 --> 16:14.830
That, or he's already got a girlfriend.

16:14.830 --> 16:16.280
I'm not listening! I hear nothing!

16:16.280 --> 16:19.030
If you ask someone you
barely know for their details,

16:19.030 --> 16:22.090
that's a 100 percent guarantee
you can't be just friends.

16:22.090 --> 16:25.120
It takes real guts and courage.

16:25.120 --> 16:28.490
I don't think she was asking
because she wanted to be friends...

16:29.160 --> 16:30.550
That's true.

16:30.550 --> 16:32.990
They're doing their best
to put it out there, huh?

16:32.990 --> 16:35.180
That'd make any guy super happy.

16:35.540 --> 16:38.620
Hear that, girls? It'd make
any guy super happy!

16:38.620 --> 16:41.560
At least try to cover up
that you don't care who it is.

16:41.870 --> 16:42.790
He's back!

16:42.790 --> 16:44.530
Hey there, hot stuff!

16:44.530 --> 16:46.560
Yagi-senpai wanted to talk to you, right?

16:46.560 --> 16:48.390
What'd she say?

16:48.390 --> 16:50.770
Oh, you know, just stuff?

16:50.770 --> 16:53.070
Sorry, don't tell anyone what you saw.

16:53.070 --> 16:54.390
'Kay.

16:54.390 --> 16:55.720
So he shot her down.

16:55.720 --> 16:57.070
How slick.

16:58.070 --> 17:00.410
I'm relieved, but my heart pains for her.

17:00.410 --> 17:06.350
If it weren't for sheer dumb luck,
I might've gotten shot down too.

17:06.350 --> 17:08.640
Hey, do you want to be friends?!

17:08.640 --> 17:09.780
Oh... Uh...

17:08.960 --> 17:09.380
Oh...

17:09.340 --> 17:09.750
Uh...

17:09.790 --> 17:13.090
I can't help but sympathize with the girls!

17:15.660 --> 17:18.220
We'll have a girls' outing
over summer break, right?

17:18.220 --> 17:20.420
We could study at someone's
house or something.

17:20.420 --> 17:21.570
That sounds great!

17:21.570 --> 17:23.700
If we do a sleepover, we could watch movies!

17:23.700 --> 17:27.680
That sounds like so much fun!
A pajama party!

17:27.680 --> 17:28.980
When do you want to do it?

17:29.740 --> 17:31.620
Mika-chan, do your parents allow sleepovers?

17:31.620 --> 17:32.490
Huh?

17:32.860 --> 17:35.390
Oh, I guess I'm included in this.

17:36.020 --> 17:36.860
Probably.

17:37.450 --> 17:40.540
Oh, are your parents strict, Makoto?

17:40.540 --> 17:42.490
Nah, it's not that.

17:42.910 --> 17:48.500
I-I just thought I was the type that'd
never be in pajama parties and stuff.

17:50.980 --> 17:53.530
Let's do all the things high school girls do!

17:53.530 --> 17:55.240
How about we don't?!

17:55.240 --> 17:56.550
There, there.

17:57.860 --> 18:00.200
It does feel a little strange,
though, doesn't it?

18:00.200 --> 18:02.840
You wouldn't think we would
all be in the same friend group.

18:04.050 --> 18:05.180
She's right.

18:06.400 --> 18:08.420
If we weren't all in the same class,

18:08.120 --> 18:09.900
Hey, where are we going?

18:08.420 --> 18:11.320
I'd never have made friends
with any of them.

18:09.900 --> 18:12.080
I wanna hang out at Shima's place.

18:12.080 --> 18:13.190
Huh? Is that a no?!

18:16.600 --> 18:19.850
Please pass these along to each class.

18:19.850 --> 18:22.780
That concludes the class officers meeting.

18:22.780 --> 18:24.700
Thank you very much.

18:26.870 --> 18:29.640
We could just mention it
in morning homeroom, right?

18:29.640 --> 18:31.230
Yeah, you're right.

18:32.090 --> 18:33.870
Speaking of mornings, today...

18:34.270 --> 18:37.120
Remember how I said the zoo
would be super crowded?

18:37.120 --> 18:38.300
Y-Yeah.

18:38.300 --> 18:41.340
I still get nervous around him, but...

18:41.340 --> 18:42.790
And what about it?

18:42.790 --> 18:44.350
W-Well, you see...

18:44.720 --> 18:45.790
I looked into it,

18:45.790 --> 18:49.130
and apparently it's not too bad on weekdays,
even during summer break.

18:49.130 --> 18:50.350
Really?

18:50.350 --> 18:52.230
Whoops, forgot something.

18:52.230 --> 18:53.420
You're right!

18:53.420 --> 18:56.610
Of course! Adults don't get summer breaks!

18:54.590 --> 18:56.610
Yikes, how am I supposed to go in there?

18:56.610 --> 19:00.610
Sorry for jumping to conclusions
and scaring you like that.

19:01.170 --> 19:02.940
He's so nice.

19:02.940 --> 19:06.740
Dumb luck or not, I'm so glad we're friends.

19:07.190 --> 19:12.720
I do fantasize about how it'd be fun for us
to go to the zoo together and stuff,

19:12.720 --> 19:15.080
but I want to treasure this friendship!

19:15.540 --> 19:17.150
Are you gonna go with anyone?

19:17.150 --> 19:19.130
Oh, about that...

19:19.130 --> 19:19.970
Do you want to go in a group?

19:19.970 --> 19:21.380
Do you want to go together?

19:27.650 --> 19:28.640
Urk.

19:28.640 --> 19:32.900
Arrrggghhh!

19:32.900 --> 19:34.140
It slipped out!

19:34.140 --> 19:35.220
Sure.

19:36.990 --> 19:38.640
Before Obon, right?

19:38.640 --> 19:40.400
When are you free?

19:40.400 --> 19:42.030
A-Are you sure?

19:42.030 --> 19:43.280
Huh? Of course.

19:43.780 --> 19:46.530
It's easier to get around in a smaller
group of two to three people.

19:47.060 --> 19:49.110
How about Thursday or Friday
the week after next?

19:49.110 --> 19:51.050
He's so casual about it.

19:51.050 --> 19:55.160
He's usually so tuned in
to what girls are thinking,

19:55.160 --> 19:57.700
A day with clear weather would be nice.

19:55.160 --> 19:59.730
but he can't read my
"Wait, isn't this a date?" aura?!

19:57.700 --> 19:59.730
Thursday or Friday...

19:59.730 --> 20:01.300
Oh, Thursday, then...

20:01.300 --> 20:04.560
It could be that when he looks at me...

20:03.760 --> 20:09.810
100% Friend

20:03.760 --> 20:09.810
Made in Ishikawa Prefecture

20:04.560 --> 20:05.620
You wanna hang out together?

20:05.620 --> 20:06.980
Okay!

20:06.980 --> 20:09.810
...that's what he sees!

20:10.140 --> 20:12.530
I've never seen a panda in real life.

20:12.530 --> 20:13.690
Really?

20:13.690 --> 20:14.630
But...

20:14.630 --> 20:17.080
I thought all Tokyo folk would've seen one.

20:17.080 --> 20:18.000
Even then...

20:18.620 --> 20:20.360
Of course not.

20:20.360 --> 20:24.320
I'm happy he doesn't mind
going places with me!

20:24.320 --> 20:26.070
Is that so?

20:29.960 --> 20:30.880
Hmph.

20:34.620 --> 20:36.580
Sorry, I'm getting a call.

20:36.580 --> 20:37.870
Hello?

20:38.900 --> 20:40.210
What? You're at the gate?

20:40.210 --> 20:43.470
Yeah. I wanted to see
what your school's like.

20:43.810 --> 20:46.290
Come on, what's the big problem?

20:46.730 --> 20:49.430
Whatever. I'll just ask this girl here.

20:49.920 --> 20:51.820
Hey, you there!

20:56.170 --> 20:59.900
Do you know which class Shima Sousuke's in?

21:01.710 --> 21:04.270
Sorry! Something came up. I gotta go!

21:04.270 --> 21:05.920
Oh, okay.

21:11.470 --> 21:12.580
Huh...

21:13.040 --> 21:14.750
This it?

21:14.750 --> 21:16.330
It's so average.

21:26.890 --> 21:29.600
M-Might you be Mika-chan's friend?

21:31.470 --> 21:33.730
I'm starting to get it.

21:35.320 --> 21:36.340
There you are!

21:36.340 --> 21:37.330
Ririka!

21:37.330 --> 21:39.480
I told you to wait at the gate!

21:39.480 --> 21:41.500
I never agreed to that.

21:41.500 --> 21:43.740
You're not allowed inside! Let's go!

21:44.160 --> 21:45.440
Bye, you two.

21:45.440 --> 21:46.240
See you tomorrow.

21:49.090 --> 21:51.030
She sure was unique.

21:51.030 --> 21:52.620
Uh, are you serious?

21:52.620 --> 21:54.540
That doesn't even begin to describe her!

21:54.540 --> 21:57.540
The Youngest HT
Cover Girl in History!
Saijou Ririka

22:05.960 --> 22:08.280
That the girl we just saw, don'cha reckon?!

22:08.280 --> 22:09.570
Yeah, I reckon!

22:27.410 --> 22:31.670
A gentle breeze, the setting sun

22:31.670 --> 22:35.990
Today was another good day

22:35.990 --> 22:40.330
Forgetting all the plans I made

22:40.330 --> 22:44.340
I'll walk to the next station over

22:44.340 --> 22:49.010
The more I trip and fall

22:49.010 --> 22:53.020
The better I get at picking myself back up

22:53.020 --> 22:57.590
Through honest dialogue and heart-to-hearts

22:57.590 --> 23:01.990
The warmth seeps into my soul

23:01.990 --> 23:06.280
Humming as I take the roundabout way

23:06.280 --> 23:10.410
My world is an unsolved mystery

23:10.410 --> 23:14.920
Top speed, toes and heels, strides

23:14.920 --> 23:19.080
Each one of us walks differently

23:19.080 --> 23:23.600
All the same, we wave goodbye to dusk

23:23.600 --> 23:27.590
As a new morning dawns

23:27.590 --> 23:32.260
Wanting to protect this everyday life

23:32.260 --> 23:35.480
With a hop, jump, and skip

23:35.480 --> 23:38.730
See you tomorrow
